WEBVTT

00:00.580 --> 00:02.110
In the present time,

00:02.600 --> 00:05.900
with VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.900 --> 00:09.010
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.950 --> 00:17.830
And there exists

00:17.830 --> 00:21.960
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:21.960 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the name of that game is...

00:26.820 --> 00:29.290
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:33.180 --> 00:34.430
However...

00:36.060 --> 00:38.310
After several heartbreaking events,

00:38.310 --> 00:40.770
Sunraku stopped playing SLF,

00:40.770 --> 00:43.520
but instead, a robot action game
in which you can customize

00:43.520 --> 00:46.510
and fight with mechs that came down
from the sky called "Nephilim."

00:46.510 --> 00:48.250
Nephilim Hollow.

01:04.170 --> 01:10.130
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:19.490 --> 02:21.790
#32: TWIN WINGS IN A DRAG

02:21.790 --> 02:22.910
#32: TWIN WINGS IN A DRAG
This player...

02:23.460 --> 02:25.670
There's no mistaking it! It's him!

02:31.550 --> 02:33.220
Crimson Twinewing...

02:33.220 --> 02:36.050
CRIMSON TWINEWING

02:36.050 --> 02:39.680
I'm really tired of seeing this Nephilim.

02:39.680 --> 02:40.560
Rust!

02:40.950 --> 02:42.950
Big news! You gotta look at this!

02:42.950 --> 02:45.060
Mordo?
What's all the racket in the morning?

02:46.310 --> 02:47.980
How could I not?

02:47.980 --> 02:49.360
It's Sunraku!

02:49.750 --> 02:52.900
That Sunraku is fighting
Super Tama-O right now!

02:56.030 --> 03:00.660
This default kingfisher-colored unit...
It's Kingfisher!

03:03.160 --> 03:06.920
I know, right! Everyone got all
fired up in the spectator chat.

03:06.920 --> 03:07.790
Have it back.

03:07.790 --> 03:10.590
Whoa, hey!
Aren't you gonna watch it?

03:10.590 --> 03:12.670
Kingfisher will win anyway.

03:12.670 --> 03:15.050
And I ain't gonna let other
players beat me to him.

03:17.050 --> 03:18.180
Let's go.

03:18.180 --> 03:21.640
The next one to fight Sunraku will be me!

03:28.020 --> 03:29.420
We had a tie...

03:29.970 --> 03:32.780
But after that ranked match,
why did you stop playing?

03:33.160 --> 03:34.150
Sunraku!

03:36.610 --> 03:38.940
Huh? Why?

03:38.940 --> 03:41.410
I dunno, I don't bother
remembering such small stuff.

03:41.950 --> 03:45.460
Maybe I found a really big trash game
to play or something.

03:46.080 --> 03:47.250
Trash game?

03:49.670 --> 03:51.290
What did you say?

03:51.290 --> 03:53.000
You stopped for that reason?!

03:53.000 --> 03:56.260
What do you mean?
It's a valid reason for me...

03:56.260 --> 03:57.510
RUST CHALLENGED YOU TO A DUEL

03:59.890 --> 04:01.930
Let's duel, Sunraku!

04:01.930 --> 04:04.680
I'll completely smash you
into pieces this time!

04:08.730 --> 04:12.230
Does every single player of this game
act like you or something?

04:12.230 --> 04:12.820
Huh?!

04:13.250 --> 04:17.200
But well, it's a request from
Miss #1 player herself.

04:17.200 --> 04:19.320
No way I could turn it down!

04:19.320 --> 04:21.120
Transporting to the spectator area.

04:21.120 --> 04:22.410
Don't just do that!

04:22.990 --> 04:25.080
What about our rematch?!

04:25.080 --> 04:27.160
Oh, it's finally starting!

04:27.160 --> 04:28.790
Dammit, she beat me to it!

04:28.790 --> 04:32.130
It's Crimson Twinewing against Kingfisher!

04:32.130 --> 04:33.340
- Sunraku was that guy who won
- Ugh, the crowd's already here.

04:33.340 --> 04:34.500
- all his ranked matches before, right?
- Ugh, the crowd's already here.

04:34.500 --> 04:35.160
That's the guy!

04:35.160 --> 04:37.360
His tie with Rust was
the only one he didn't win!

04:38.090 --> 04:39.300
Mordo?

04:40.370 --> 04:43.010
Not playing around, eh?

04:44.180 --> 04:46.970
Nobody was able to corner
my Crimson Twinewing

04:47.410 --> 04:50.230
as much as his Kingfisher.

04:50.810 --> 04:53.110
The time's finally here!

04:53.110 --> 04:56.440
Kingfisher versus Crimson Twinewing!

04:56.440 --> 04:58.120
Duel Start!

05:05.490 --> 05:06.660
Here I go, Sunraku!

05:07.160 --> 05:08.870
It's started!

05:47.490 --> 05:48.700
You're not getting away!

06:26.370 --> 06:29.240
Here's my payback for earlier!

06:29.240 --> 06:30.450
Not happening!

06:30.450 --> 06:32.660
Whoa, scary!

07:28.390 --> 07:29.800
They're so fast!

07:29.800 --> 07:32.810
What's going on
with their sense of balance?!

07:35.850 --> 07:42.190
It's not an exaggeration to say that I play
this game to knock Rust off the #1 spot.

07:42.980 --> 07:46.110
Even now, I'm certain that I can do it.

07:46.110 --> 07:47.820
I'll beat her someday.

07:48.490 --> 07:49.780
But...

07:49.780 --> 07:53.870
I hate to say it, but you are probably
the closest one to her right now!

08:09.930 --> 08:13.890
Go get her, Sunraku!

08:15.270 --> 08:16.270
Kick her ass—

08:21.730 --> 08:22.770
What?!

08:23.900 --> 08:27.280
WINNER CRIMSON TWINEWING

08:29.030 --> 08:30.280
Huh?

08:31.870 --> 08:34.660
Argh, I was too bold in my offense.

08:34.660 --> 08:36.830
Her moves were totally unpredictable.

08:36.830 --> 08:38.790
What is she, a super ball?

08:38.790 --> 08:40.250
Sunraku...

08:40.750 --> 08:42.030
You little...

08:42.030 --> 08:42.670
Huh?

08:43.210 --> 08:47.550
How could you let that attack hit you?!
Take this seriously!

08:47.930 --> 08:50.090
Huh? Don't be stupid!

08:50.090 --> 08:52.720
I haven't played this game
for three months!

08:52.720 --> 08:56.810
How am I supposed to adapt immediately
to such a crazy highspeed battle?

08:56.810 --> 08:58.060
What did you say?!

08:58.410 --> 09:02.730
Besides, you know, I gotta
rethink my custom job and all.

09:02.730 --> 09:06.820
I heard they added some new parts,
and I'm sure the trends have changed.

09:08.900 --> 09:11.990
One more time! Let's fight again!

09:12.570 --> 09:15.620
I know! You can just fight me
to get you up to speed!

09:15.620 --> 09:18.580
No way.
You'll just mercilessly destroy my units.

09:19.210 --> 09:20.590
What's wrong with that?!

09:20.590 --> 09:22.250
There's no point in holding back in a—

09:22.250 --> 09:25.350
Rust! Calm down!
Everyone's watching!

09:27.210 --> 09:30.300
It's sure rare to see
Rust raise her voice.

09:30.300 --> 09:32.520
Wow, I've never seen her like that.

09:32.520 --> 09:34.300
She usually acts cool and collected.

09:35.430 --> 09:38.140
I'm sorry for that.

09:38.140 --> 09:40.230
She just got a little carried away.

09:40.230 --> 09:42.440
She's actually just really
happy to see you back—

09:42.440 --> 09:42.900
Shut up!

09:46.190 --> 09:49.240
All right. I'll finish up
my Nephilim today.

09:51.210 --> 09:53.860
How about a rematch tomorrow morning?

09:57.490 --> 09:59.660
Hey, what about our rematch?!

10:00.580 --> 10:01.540
Fine.

10:02.120 --> 10:05.670
But if you dare to put in
a lame performance like that again...

10:05.670 --> 10:06.710
I'll make you pay.

10:08.670 --> 10:09.880
Let's go, Mordo.

10:11.300 --> 10:12.550
Excuse us!

10:13.550 --> 10:16.220
Make me pay how, I wonder.

10:16.890 --> 10:20.640
Also, she's using the same unit
from three months ago.

10:20.640 --> 10:22.980
She's been using the same setup
this whole time?

10:22.980 --> 10:26.520
You really don't know
anything about her, don't you?

10:26.520 --> 10:27.610
Huh?

10:27.610 --> 10:29.650
Until someone beats her,

10:29.650 --> 10:33.950
she'd stick with the same setup.
That's her strange policy.

10:34.740 --> 10:38.870
Does that mean nobody's beaten her
since my last login?

10:38.870 --> 10:40.200
Yeah.

10:40.200 --> 10:44.500
She was challenged by all sorts of players
but remains undefeated.

10:44.500 --> 10:45.880
It pisses me off.

10:46.420 --> 10:49.500
So she's invincible online, huh?

10:51.090 --> 10:52.510
All right! I've decided!

10:53.800 --> 10:58.220
I'm gonna keep playing Nephilim until
I make her rehaul her Crimson Twinewing!

10:59.190 --> 11:00.180
Sunraku.

11:01.430 --> 11:03.480
If you let me fight you again...

11:04.060 --> 11:07.730
...I'd be happy to tell you
the key to Rust's strength.

11:07.730 --> 11:09.320
NEPHILIM HOLLOW

11:09.320 --> 11:10.980
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:11.530 --> 11:13.820
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:13.820 --> 11:16.490
NEPHILIM HOLLOW

11:25.000 --> 11:28.920
One day, the first titan
fell into the world.

11:33.050 --> 11:36.720
The titan went on a rampage
and destroyed the capital...

11:41.810 --> 11:45.730
It spread its breath across the land
and blew itself to death in the end.

11:48.400 --> 11:52.860
The threat seemed to have ended,
but it was only the start.

11:52.860 --> 11:56.530
Titans continued to come flying in
across the planet...

12:01.780 --> 12:05.200
...and eventually destroyed
around half of the civilization.

12:05.670 --> 12:09.960
Cornered, humanity discovered
a certain technology.

12:10.830 --> 12:12.170
And that is...

12:18.760 --> 12:21.850
...the fusion of titans and humans.

12:23.640 --> 12:25.890
The First Nephilim War...

12:26.430 --> 12:31.060
"Two hundred years passed
since the battle between

12:31.060 --> 12:34.860
human-driven titans
and the rampaging titans," huh?

12:34.860 --> 12:37.740
Oh, right. This was the backstory.

12:37.740 --> 12:40.490
I skipped the opening, so I forgot.

12:40.490 --> 12:42.300
Whatcha doing over there?

12:42.300 --> 12:44.870
You're going to build a Nephilim
to take down Rust, right?

12:45.370 --> 12:46.370
There, look.

12:47.290 --> 12:49.290
It's the furthest one on the back.

12:50.370 --> 12:53.250
Oh. Yeah,
I've never seen that type before.

12:53.250 --> 12:56.630
So that's the new base body
added in the last update?

12:56.630 --> 12:58.260
Yeah, but...

12:58.880 --> 13:01.760
It's got a lot of quirks
and faults that stick out.

13:01.760 --> 13:04.510
Almost nobody uses them.

13:04.510 --> 13:07.270
Are you really going to customize that?

13:07.270 --> 13:11.520
I've got no chance of facing Rust
in a straight-on speed duel.

13:11.520 --> 13:16.230
Besides, the fact that almost
nobody uses them is an advantage.

13:16.230 --> 13:18.650
It means nobody's explored it yet.

13:22.030 --> 13:26.830
There are three steps
in building a new Nephilim.

13:26.830 --> 13:30.410
The first is to capture a wild Nephilim.

13:32.080 --> 13:34.670
Most of the Nephilims that fell from the sky

13:34.670 --> 13:36.050
are the "open-eyes" type.

13:36.050 --> 13:37.550
OPEN-EYES TYPE
are the "open-eyes" type.

13:38.340 --> 13:42.760
This type will attack
the players as an enemy.

13:44.260 --> 13:45.850
But on rare occasions,

13:45.850 --> 13:48.100
you'll find a "closed-eyes" Nephilim.

13:48.100 --> 13:51.100
CLOSED-EYES TYPE
you'll find a "closed-eyes" Nephilim.

14:00.650 --> 14:07.200
These "closed-eyes" types are the ones the players
can control and use as a base body.

14:10.580 --> 14:12.080
"CLOSED-EYES UNIT" CAPTURED

14:12.080 --> 14:15.080
All right! I got one!

14:15.710 --> 14:17.630
Nice skills.

14:18.670 --> 14:22.470
The next step is to dress up
the naked Nephilim you captured.

14:23.050 --> 14:25.640
In other words, you customize it
with weapons and armor.

14:26.220 --> 14:30.720
You can get said parts from facilities,
the black market, or other players.

14:30.720 --> 14:32.230
Oh, Sunraku!

14:33.020 --> 14:35.350
Building a new Nephilim already?

14:35.350 --> 14:36.690
Yeah, kinda.

14:36.690 --> 14:40.610
I'd love to know what it's like,
but I'll save that up for tomorrow.

14:40.610 --> 14:42.610
You gotta beat Rust for us, man!

14:42.610 --> 14:44.360
We're all counting on ya!

14:44.360 --> 14:47.750
To be frank, I don't have much hope
for Super Tama-O.

14:47.750 --> 14:50.370
That's something to say against
someone stronger than you!

14:51.370 --> 14:52.330
See you guys later!

14:52.330 --> 14:53.830
Best of luck!

14:55.130 --> 14:57.040
Tch, cocky bastards.

14:57.840 --> 15:00.130
Do people hate Rust or something?

15:00.130 --> 15:02.380
Huh? Nah.

15:02.380 --> 15:04.880
Many respect her as a player.

15:06.260 --> 15:08.100
That's why we want someone to beat her.

15:08.720 --> 15:12.770
Remember what I told you?
Rust won't change her unit until she loses.

15:13.430 --> 15:19.520
People want to see Rust fighting with
something other than Crimson Twinewing.

15:20.190 --> 15:21.900
I see.

15:21.900 --> 15:24.320
So that's why you're helping me out.

15:24.320 --> 15:26.030
- What?
- Nothing.

15:26.740 --> 15:30.910
Anyway, have you come up
with a setup that could beat her?

15:30.910 --> 15:33.540
It's not that simple.

15:33.540 --> 15:37.620
Crimson Twinewing's unpredictable movements
are a far cry from Kingfisher's.

15:38.000 --> 15:40.530
Reaction, response, and control...

15:40.530 --> 15:42.670
Rust is off the charts in all aspects.

15:42.670 --> 15:45.340
She's not the champion for nothing.

15:45.340 --> 15:48.680
And the other problem is
in the info you gave me.

15:48.680 --> 15:49.390
Huh?

15:49.390 --> 15:53.890
This "Mordo" guy is telling
Rust my movements, right?

15:53.890 --> 15:57.060
Mordo is a skilled operator assistant.

15:57.060 --> 16:00.270
Your run-of-the-mill tricks
won't work on him.

16:01.110 --> 16:04.030
And that's the key
to Rust's strength, huh?

16:05.030 --> 16:08.660
Then maybe I have to
pry in on Rust herself.

16:10.410 --> 16:12.660
Hey, lemme see some leg parts.

16:12.660 --> 16:15.120
Sure thing. They're in warehouse C4.

16:15.120 --> 16:16.540
Hey, Sunraku?

16:17.960 --> 16:21.710
I've got an idea for an "anti-Rust Nephilim."

16:38.940 --> 16:43.190
Whoa, whoa! Is Nephilim's
entire player base here or what?

16:43.190 --> 16:45.860
How long has it been
since we had this many players together?

16:45.860 --> 16:47.820
I was so excited I couldn't sleep.

16:47.820 --> 16:49.450
Is Sunraku there yet?

16:49.450 --> 16:51.240
Hey, move! I can't see behind you!

16:51.240 --> 16:52.570
When's it gonna start?

16:57.080 --> 16:57.960
There he is.

17:10.010 --> 17:11.800
Hey. Sorry I'm late.

17:13.100 --> 17:14.970
So that's your new unit?

17:15.470 --> 17:18.060
Sure is! Cool, don't cha think?

17:18.810 --> 17:23.230
The final step, give a name
to the Nephilim you build.

17:23.230 --> 17:24.940
I call it...

17:26.150 --> 17:27.890
The Fiddler Crab.

17:27.890 --> 17:29.950
FIDDLER CRAB

17:30.240 --> 17:36.910
Unlike Kingfisher, it's a heavily armored,
heavy-weight Nephilim.

17:36.910 --> 17:38.580
Is he pitting that against me?

17:38.580 --> 17:40.410
Fiddler Crab...

17:40.410 --> 17:42.960
It's the name of a type of crab, right?

17:44.920 --> 17:48.590
As the name implies,
it's got a pincher like a fiddle crab's.

17:49.670 --> 17:54.140
V6 Slicing Pincer Unit, Bookmaker.

17:54.140 --> 17:56.560
It deals massive damage in a single attack,

17:56.560 --> 17:59.350
but its reach is limited
and has a low attack speed.

17:59.350 --> 18:04.350
I wouldn't call it effective against
a high-speed unit like Crimson Twinewing.

18:05.980 --> 18:07.610
What is he up to?

18:08.150 --> 18:12.030
Well, Mordo.
Think you can figure it out?

18:12.030 --> 18:13.740
Sunraku's trump card.

18:14.230 --> 18:15.870
Why are you acting all smug about it?

18:15.870 --> 18:17.910
Don't forget you're "Super Tama-O."

18:17.910 --> 18:18.740
Shut up.

18:20.160 --> 18:21.250
Rust.

18:22.160 --> 18:23.790
If you judge the book by its cover,

18:23.790 --> 18:27.250
this thing will sink your
Crimson Twinewing in an instant.

18:31.760 --> 18:33.970
I look forward to that.

18:33.970 --> 18:36.800
Let's get this started
right away, Sunraku.

18:39.060 --> 18:42.310
I'll end this in a flash, Rust.

19:00.830 --> 19:03.870
Fiddler Crab versus Crimson Twinewing!

19:03.870 --> 19:05.790
Duel Start!

19:34.240 --> 19:35.150
You don't see that booster legs often.

19:35.150 --> 19:37.780
BOOSTER LEGS
You don't see that booster legs often.

19:37.780 --> 19:40.780
It's got a minimum of mobility, at least.

19:48.130 --> 19:51.500
But that bookmaker he got
as a main weapon...

19:51.500 --> 19:55.170
It's not a weapon you'd pick against
Crimson Twinewing without a plan.

19:55.170 --> 19:56.510
He's got to have a plan.

19:59.680 --> 20:02.010
Rust, that head part he's using...

20:02.010 --> 20:03.180
I know.

20:03.180 --> 20:05.270
He's using a pretty obscure build.

20:10.440 --> 20:15.110
You think you can faze me
just by using some uncommon parts?!

20:17.150 --> 20:18.700
We'll see.

20:21.830 --> 20:22.970
He vanished?!

20:23.960 --> 20:25.750
It's optical camo.

20:25.750 --> 20:29.790
He can go invisible for a few seconds
if he doesn't perform an attack motion.

20:29.790 --> 20:34.300
Oh, yeah! That head part is an optical camo!
I totally forgot about it!

20:34.300 --> 20:36.630
Nobody uses 'em anymore, after all.

20:36.630 --> 20:37.800
Yeah.

20:37.800 --> 20:40.340
Because optical camo in Nephilim...

20:40.970 --> 20:43.600
Yeah, it's got a major flaw to it.

20:54.610 --> 20:59.240
The only thing optical camo
conceals is the robot itself.

20:59.240 --> 21:02.280
It cannot cover the blast visual effect
from his booster legs.

21:02.950 --> 21:05.740
With the booster firing angles
of his Nephilim and the dust

21:05.740 --> 21:09.120
I can read his Nephilim's
moves like a book!

21:12.250 --> 21:15.880
Right there! Better luck
next time, Fiddler Crab!

21:22.430 --> 21:24.140
Something's odd.

21:24.140 --> 21:27.270
I seriously doubt he couldn't
anticipate this happening.

21:27.670 --> 21:30.620
He went out of his way to use
uncommon parts for this.

21:30.620 --> 21:32.270
He can't be taken down this easily.

21:37.400 --> 21:40.150
I don't see traces of him
escaping with his booster...

21:47.530 --> 21:49.410
No way, that Nephilim...!

21:49.410 --> 21:51.290
Rust! Get away from there!

21:56.000 --> 21:57.000
It's over.

22:03.090 --> 22:04.090
Heh!
